  "analytical_usefulness": 0.83,
  "source_groundedness": 0.76,
  "rationale": "The added columns decompose the free-text reviews into distinct, satisfaction-relevant service dimensions (crew, meals, seat, ground ops, customer service), each offering a real axis to group and model Overall Rating on—directly serving the driver-analysis query. seat_comfort_adequacy is the weakest for usefulness given overlap with the existing Seat Comfort rating. Groundedness is generally good: silent rows are correctly marked Unknown/NULL rather than fabricated, but several rows show confident category assignments (e.g., crew labeled dismissive/polite or seat labeled cramped) where the source text is silent or only weakly supportive, indicating occasional unwarranted specifics."
